<section class="hero"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">Natural cork marine decking</span><h1>A Better Decking Experience. Naturally.</h1><p>Explore Jelinek AquaCork marine decking—a natural alternative designed for comfort, traction, and a distinctive finish on the water.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="#contact">Request a Decking Consultation</a><a class="button outline" href="#benefits">Explore Benefits</a></div></div></section>
<section id="benefits" class="wrap section"><div class="center"><span class="eyebrow">Why AquaCork</span><h2>Comfort that belongs on the water.</h2><p>A thoughtfully selected marine decking material can change how your vessel looks and feels.</p></div><div class="grid">
<article><b>01 / COMFORT</b><h3>Comfort underfoot</h3><p>Cork's resilient character offers a welcoming surface for time spent aboard.</p></article>
<article><b>02 / TRACTION</b><h3>Designed for wet decks</h3><p>Jelinek describes AquaCork as a non-skid marine decking option. No surface is slip-proof.</p></article>
<article><b>03 / CLIMATE</b><h3>Thermal comfort</h3><p>Explore the manufacturer-described thermal benefits of cork in sunny marine environments.</p></article>
<article><b>04 / STYLE</b><h3>Natural warmth</h3><p>Warm cork tones bring a refined appearance to your vessel.</p></article>
<article><b>05 / QUIET</b><h3>Sound and vibration</h3><p>Cork is valued for sound- and vibration-dampening properties.</p></article>
<article><b>06 / MATERIAL</b><h3>Renewable cork</h3><p>Cork bark can be harvested without felling the cork oak tree.</p></article>
</div></section>
<section id="process" class="dark section"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">Our approach</span><h2>Precision from planning to the final detail.</h2><p>Every vessel is different. Our proposed process puts careful assessment and manufacturer-approved installation requirements first.</p><div class="steps"><div><b>01</b><h3>Consult</h3><p>Discuss your goals.</p></div><div><b>02</b><h3>Measure</h3><p>Plan the layout.</p></div><div><b>03</b><h3>Prepare</h3><p>Evaluate the substrate.</p></div><div><b>04</b><h3>Install</h3><p>Follow approved methods.</p></div><div><b>05</b><h3>Review</h3><p>Discuss care and maintenance.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section id="applications" class="wrap section"><span class="eyebrow">Applications & inspiration</span><h2>Made for the places you enjoy most.</h2><p>Explore decking possibilities for cockpits, aft decks, swim platforms, walkways, and steps, subject to suitability.</p><div class="gallery"><div>Aft decks & cockpits</div><div>Swim platforms</div><div>Steps & walkways</div></div><p class="note">Design placeholders only. Genuine installation photography will be added with permission.</p></section>
